  "note": "番坊码头、船工棚 (native:fanfang/dock, shed; 番坊 A): the port at the sea cliff's foot — the steps come down at the north-west onto a quay of big worn stones crusted white with salt, crates and bales up from the boats, salt in sacks waiting for the porters, a derrick, the 市舶司's table with its ledger and steelyard under a lantern; two wooden jetties on piles out into a grey-blue sea, three flat-bottomed boats with mat sails rolled tied up beside them (the boats are others': theme:4); west under the cliff the boatmen's thatched lean-to with nets drying, oars, coils of rope and a pot of fish soup on stones; gulls on the posts. Old and used: tar and fish-scale stains, broken crates, a net torn and patched, weed on the piles.",
